      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://neuracryption.com#faq",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does quick call center setup in 3 minutes work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Quick call center setup takes under 180 seconds on NeuraCryption with our 3-step dashboard workflow. First, navigate to Call Center in the dashboard and click Provision Call Center Number. Second, select your country (US or Canada), choose a Local Number or Toll-Free Number (800/888/877), and claim an available line for a flat $2.00 one-time fee. Third, configure your AI persona in context.md or pick a 1-click starter template (Customer Support, Appointment Scheduler, Sales Lead Qualifier). Your line is immediately active with an automated webhook to handle incoming calls or dial outbound calls."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can NeuraCryption handle both inbound customer support and outbound sales calling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. NeuraCryption is natively calibrated to recognize call direction dynamically. When an inbound call arrives, the AI acts as an empathetic support agent or receptionist. When dialing outbound, the AI dynamically adopts an outbound posture, utilizing structured, permission-based openers to engage prospects, qualify leads, and convert conversations."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does the Outbound Autodialer and Batch CSV Campaign feature work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Every provisioned line includes an integrated Outbound Autodialer for immediate 1-click dialing. For mass outreach, click Batch Campaign (CSV Autodialer), enter your campaign name, and upload a standard CSV file with Name and Phone columns. The AI automatically dials through your contact list, navigates conversations, and logs call outcomes in real time."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What native tools are included, and do they cost extra?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "You do not pay a single penny extra for tools. NeuraCryption includes four native suites integrated directly into our backend: AI Calendar & Booking for scheduling, NeuraDocs Suite for rich text notes, NeuraSheets Suite for automated data logging, and NeuraEmail Suite for caller identity verification and follow-up emails. You orchestrate any of these tools simply by referencing them in your context.md prompt."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I customize my AI agent persona using context.md?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Inside your line configuration, you have a dedicated context.md prompt editor (up to 500 lines) with starter templates for Customer Support Agent, Appointment Scheduler, and Inbound Sales Lead Qualifier. Define your agent's identity, conversational warmth, identity verification checkpoints, and function triggers in plain text."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What phone numbers can I provision, and what is the pricing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "You can provision direct Local Numbers or Toll-Free Numbers (800, 888, 877 prefixes) across the United States and Canada with instant 1-click purchasing at a flat $2.00 one-time setup fee per number. There are zero monthly seat licenses or hidden line rental markups; you only pay for active compute talk-time starting at $0.05 per minute."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does the AI handle customer interruptions and conversational pauses?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "NeuraCryption features ultra-low sub-500ms voice inference paired with real-time Voice Activity Detection (VAD). When a caller interrupts or speaks mid-sentence, the AI cuts off audio generation in milliseconds, preserves conversational context, and listens attentively, eliminating robotic talkover."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I test the AI voice model before signing up or depositing funds?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. We offer an open, no-login interactive demo at neuracryption.com/demo where you can speak live with our voice agent in your browser. Additionally, for qualified businesses ready to deploy, we are offering 10 fully funded pilot accounts with $200 in free compute credit. Contact enterprise@neuracryption.com to apply."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does NeuraCryption compare to building directly with the raw Gemini Live API?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "As documented in our published research whitepaper, stateful multimodal WebSockets in Gemini Live re-process accumulated raw audio tokens on every conversational turn, compounding costs quadratically. A 30-minute call under Gemini Live can reach $29.42, whereas NeuraCryption charges a flat rate of just $2.40 ($0.08/min) with telecom routing included."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why choose NeuraCryption over building a fragmented multi-vendor voice stack?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Assembling a conventional voice pipeline requires configuring, maintaining, and paying for separate third-party services: carrier telephony, speech recognition, LLM reasoning, and audio synthesis. That fragmented multi-hop architecture introduces network latency delays and compounding fees of $0.13 to $0.28 per minute. NeuraCryption replaces this complex engineering with a unified, full-stack autonomous telecom utility: 3-minute setup, 85 languages with native auto-detection, sub-500ms voice latency, and a transparent flat compute rate starting from $0.05 per minute."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
